@cc ===========================================================================
@cc SPLITC - compile TWO modules SEPARATELY and link them into one program.
@cc
@cc This is the whole point of the exercise: each COMPILE produces its own BRF,
@cc and the linker joins them. If this works, CHAT.PLNC can be split so that
@cc editing one part recompiles one part - twenty minutes becomes a few.
@cc
@cc THE ORDER INSIDE THE LINKER IS: the program first, THEN the libraries that
@cc satisfy it. Same rule as the chat build.
@cc ===========================================================================

@cc --- clear the old build; NO SUCH FILE NAME on a first run is expected -----
@DELETE-FILE SPLIT:PROG
@DELETE-FILE SPLITA:BRF
@DELETE-FILE SPLITB:BRF
@DELETE-FILE SPLITA:LIST
@DELETE-FILE SPLITB:LIST

@cc --- compile each module on its own ---------------------------------------
@cc Quoting: no quotes means the file must already exist, "quotes" means create.
@PLANC-100-F00
COMPILE SPLITA:PLNC,"SPLITA:LIST","SPLITA"
EXIT

@PLANC-100-F00
COMPILE SPLITB:PLNC,"SPLITB:LIST","SPLITB"
EXIT

@cc --- link the two objects together ----------------------------------------
@cc SPLITB holds the PROGRAM, so it goes first; SPLITA is what it needs.
@cc LIST-ENTRIES-UNDEFINED is the test that every cross-module name resolved -
@cc a name that did not survive the seven-character BRF limit shows up here and
@cc NOWHERE else.
@BRF-LINKER-C01
PROGRAM-FILE "SPLIT"
LOAD SPLITB
LOAD SPLITA
LIBRARY-MODE ON
LOAD PLANC-1BANK-F00
LIST-ENTRIES-UNDEFINED
EXIT

@cc ===========================================================================
@cc Built SPLIT:PROG. Run it with @SPLIT
@cc
@cc   counter 43, text HELLO   -> shared data works, the split is safe
@cc   counter 0 or blank text  -> each module got its OWN copy; the split
@cc                               cannot share state and CHAT.PLNC would have
@cc                               to pass it in parameters instead
@cc
@cc Check BOTH listings for "*** ERROR" before believing anything.
@cc ===========================================================================
